        definition: "The log-likelihood of logistic regression is ℓ(w) = Σᵢ [yᵢ log σ(wᵀxᵢ) + (1 − yᵢ) log(1 − σ(wᵀxᵢ))]. Its gradient is ∇ℓ(w) = Σᵢ (yᵢ − σ(wᵀxᵢ)) xᵢ = X(y − σ(Xᵀw)). There is no closed-form maximiser, so w is found iteratively by gradient ascent: w ← w + η∇ℓ(w).",
